@@ -105,8 +105,8 @@ tensor-booster OOF cache contains exactly 1,320 supported samples
 their validation tensors retain about 218 MiB of tensor payload after the full
 inner-training splits are released.
 
-The exhaustive CP grid requires 240 inner structural decompositions per task
-(`5 ranks x 2 caps x 2 initializations x 3 seeds x 4 folds`) plus three selected
+The exhaustive CP grid requires 360 inner structural decompositions per task
+(`5 ranks x 3 caps x 2 initializations x 3 seeds x 4 folds`) plus three selected
 outer refits. Tucker requires 768 inner representations
 (`4 input ranks x 4 output ranks x 2 caps x 2 initializations x 3 seeds x
 4 folds`), each with one input and one output decomposition, plus three outer
@@ -114,9 +114,9 @@ representations. Regularization heads reuse each structural representation,
 and the representation cache is evicted before the next structural group.
 
 The full development manifest contains 45 family-fold tasks. It accounts for
-1,532 declared family trials per outer fold plus nine reference-Ridge trials in
-each of the CP and Tucker tasks: 1,550 checkpointed trial records per fold and
-4,650 across development. Outer prediction arrays are approximately 20 MiB
+1,593 declared family trials per outer fold plus ten reference-Ridge trials in
+each of the CP and Tucker tasks: 1,613 checkpointed trial records per fold and
+4,839 across development. Outer prediction arrays are approximately 20 MiB
 uncompressed for deterministic tasks and 33 MiB for three-seed tasks, or about
 1.1 GiB across all 45 tasks before NPZ compression. Consolidated gzip search
 records, diagnostics, ledgers, and temporary restart checkpoints are expected
diff --git a/logs/RESEARCH_LOG.md b/logs/RESEARCH_LOG.md
index f5f7bda..6371049 100644
--- a/logs/RESEARCH_LOG.md
+++ b/logs/RESEARCH_LOG.md
@@ -843,3 +843,26 @@
   heads during outer replay, and records the convention in diagnostics. No
   economic result or protected period informed the change. The complete local
   code-only suite passed with `420 passed in 21.19s`.
+- Published immutable development-only manifest
+  `taq5m-dev-v3-stagea-900e1e0` at source commit
+  `900e1e047705fe75dca9fe02a68e6b48f3b06b71` and launched only its four
+  prespecified `dev-2020` resource pilots. Factor Ridge completed all 72 trials
+  with `OUTER_EVALUATED` and no search-boundary flag. CP accounted for all 120
+  trials but returned `INSUFFICIENT_VALID_TRIALS`: all 60 configurations at the
+  500-iteration cap were valid, while 30 of the 60 configurations at the
+  250-iteration cap failed the all-seed convergence gate. Tucker returned
+  `NO_VALID_CONFIGURATION` because every configuration reached the same
+  mask-handling defect before a valid fit: completely unobserved residual
+  samples were sent to the spatial output-score solve. Outer validation was
+  never opened for either tensor family, and candidate/final access remained
+  false.
+- The blocked manifest cannot support resource approval, so its sole remaining
+  gradient-boosting pilot was stopped after 144/864 durable checkpoints rather
+  than spending another projected 15 hours on an unusable experiment identity.
+  All partial and terminal artifacts were preserved. Tucker now excludes only
+  fully unobserved samples from output-score and Ridge-head training, records
+  the excluded count, and still predicts every validation sample. The CP grid
+  preserves the failed 250 cap and fully valid 500 cap and adds a 1000 cap for
+  a prespecified high-cap stability comparison; the minimum-valid threshold is
+  unchanged. These remediations use resource/convergence evidence only, not
+  outer tensor forecasts, economics, candidate data, or final-holdout data.
